# Database rules

## Clients

- Browser: `src/lib/supabase/browser.ts` (publishable key only)
- Server (user session): `src/lib/supabase/server.ts`
- Admin/service: `src/lib/supabase/server-admin.ts` (service role — never import in client components)

## Schema workflow

- SQL lives in `supabase/*.sql` as **additive** scripts for the Supabase SQL Editor
- Do not run migrations from the agent unless the user explicitly requests it
- Prefer `create table if not exists`, additive columns, and non-destructive updates
- Document any new script the operator must run

## Core domains (do not reinvent)

- Researchers, publications, projects, collaborations, scholarly metrics
- Fundings (+ detail images, attachment text, storage)
- Research news, analytics views
- `researcher_expertise_profiles` (`ai_profile`, `display_profile`, `display_origin`, `analysis_status`)
- AI vector / embeddings schema

## Profile contract

- Writes go through `src/lib/expertise/repository.ts` patterns
- Admin-locked / `display_origin = admin` must not be blindly overwritten by re-analysis
- Public matching uses `display_profile` only (`selectProfileForMatching`)

## Security

- Preserve RLS policies already defined in SQL
- Admin mutations require `requireAdminSession` / existing action guards
- Never commit `.env.local` or put secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`
- Avoid weakening public write policies

## Repositories

- Extend existing `*-repository.ts` helpers instead of parallel data layers
- Handle schema-fallback patterns already used in the codebase when columns may be missing
